+@ Optional reusable adapter. The map owner may point the Station host here.
+@ Other gyms need their own approved trainer/adapter; listed names do not grant stamps.
+TaichungGym_EventScript_StationChallenge::
+	lock
+	faceplayer
+	setvar VAR_0x8004, TAICHUNG_GYM_OLD_STATION
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptIsComplete
+	goto_if_eq VAR_RESULT, TRUE, TaichungGym_StationAlreadyComplete
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_OFFER
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptGetStationMessage
+	msgbox gStringVar4, MSGBOX_YESNO
+	goto_if_eq VAR_RESULT, NO, TaichungGym_StationDeclined
+	setvar VAR_0x8004, TAICHUNG_GYM_OLD_STATION
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TRAINER_TAICHUNG_STATION_JUN
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptPrepareChallenge
+	goto_if_eq VAR_RESULT, FALSE, TaichungGym_StationUnavailable
+	goto_if_eq VAR_0x40FB, 2, TaichungGym_StationBattleChinese
+	trainerbattle_single TRAINER_TAICHUNG_STATION_JUN, TaichungGym_Text_StationIntroEn, TaichungGym_Text_StationDefeatEn, TaichungGym_StationAfterBattle
+	goto TaichungGym_StationBattleSkipped
+
+TaichungGym_StationBattleChinese::
+	trainerbattle_single TRAINER_TAICHUNG_STATION_JUN, TaichungGym_Text_StationIntroZh, TaichungGym_Text_StationDefeatZh, TaichungGym_StationAfterBattle
+	goto TaichungGym_StationBattleSkipped
+
+@ Native trainer flags can bypass a battle (for example, a quest-log replay).
+@ Cancel tracking and release controls rather than trusting an old battle result.
+TaichungGym_StationBattleSkipped::
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptCancelChallenge
+	goto TaichungGym_StationNotRecorded
+
+TaichungGym_StationAfterBattle::
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptGetResult
+	goto_if_ne VAR_RESULT, TAICHUNG_GYM_RESULT_WON, TaichungGym_StationNotRecorded
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_COMPLETE
+	goto TaichungGym_StationMessage
+
+TaichungGym_StationAlreadyComplete::
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_ALREADY_COMPLETE
+	goto TaichungGym_StationMessage
+
+TaichungGym_StationDeclined::
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_DECLINED
+	goto TaichungGym_StationMessage
+
+TaichungGym_StationUnavailable::
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_UNAVAILABLE
+	goto TaichungGym_StationMessage
+
+TaichungGym_StationNotRecorded::
+	setvar VAR_0x8005, TAICHUNG_GYM_MESSAGE_NOT_RECORDED
+
+TaichungGym_StationMessage::
+	callnative TaichungGym_ScriptGetStationMessage
+	msgbox gStringVar4
+	release
+	end
diff --git a/data/taichung/landmarks/old-station/art-brief.md b/data/taichung/landmarks/old-station/art-brief.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..54aafc4
--- /dev/null
+++ b/data/taichung/landmarks/old-station/art-brief.md
@@ -0,0 +1,114 @@
+# Old Taichung Station: first custom landmark study
+
+Status: reference and art study. The current in-game facade still uses a copied
+Pewter museum blockout. This package does not replace any native map, door,
+tileset or script. Root owns generation review and native registration.
+
+The target is recognition from the building silhouette before reading a sign.
+Use the official frontal heritage photograph as the primary architecture source;
+the film-assistance oblique photograph clarifies pitched roof depth and the low
+canopy. The native screenshot supplies rendering style only. Exact URLs and local
+reference paths are recorded in `references.json`; downloaded photographs remain
+in isolated artifacts and are not packaged as game art.
+
+## Features that carry identity
+
+Preserve the central clock tower with white clock face and dark-green cap, the
+raised central gable, slate/charcoal hipped roofs, red brick with cream bands and
+pilasters, tall central arched window, low symmetric wings and shallow olive-gray
+front canopy. These were inspected in the official photographs. A red roof or an
+extra story would weaken identification. Tiny stone ornament, exact window counts,
+posters, signage and people can be omitted in this first pixel-art study.
+
+The full facade is south facing in the FireRed north-up overworld projection. Roof
+depth is visible from above while the front remains horizontal. Keep the original
+facade's broad low proportions, with the tower as the only strong vertical accent.
+
+## Native placement and reservation
+
+`placement.json` reserves a12×8-metatile rendering envelope: global(26,57) through
+(37,64), logical192×128 pixels. The original11×7 placeholder is(27,58) through
+(37,64). This proposal expands only north and west; it remains inside the current
+map and leaves the east boundary tree column untouched.
+
+Keep the active exterior door at global(32,64), local(6,7), native warp0/elevation0.
+The visual central opening may span columns5–6, but only the existing right-column
+warp is active until Main explicitly changes that contract. Keep approach(32,65)
+and arrival(30,66) clear at elevation3. The gym interior and its three return warps
+retain their current IDs. The nearby guide and sign at(28,66)/(29,66) are untouched.
+
+Artwork, collision and warp behavior are separate outputs. The draft blocked mask
+leaves the transparent upper corners walkable and blocks the tower/body cells;
+the integrator must reconcile it against the final silhouette and source layers.
+The animated door keeps collision1/elevation0 and `MB_WARP_DOOR` behavior. Native
+entry deliberately handles opening through that blocked tile. Other solid building
+tiles use collision1; clear exterior paths retain elevation3. No artwork or collision
+may extend south into the approach row.
+
+For the first native integration, retain the existing General0x03D animated door
+cell. If a bespoke door is wanted, author a separate door animation/table mapping
+and palette assignment: `src/field_door.c` selects animation graphics by metatile
+ID. Changing only a door's painted closed image can cause a mismatched animation;
+changing the shared General door graphics would also affect other buildings.
+
+## Color and tile budget
+
+Target at most224 unique8×8 building graphics, leaving at least160 of the384
+secondary graphic slots for neighborhood assets. Deduplicate repeated roof
+clusters, window units, brick courses and stone bands; permit horizontal flips
+where the lighting remains coherent. At most96 new16×16 metatile definitions are
+needed for the full rendering envelope; the final count can be lower through reuse.
+
+Use two secondary palette banks as a target, with exact bank IDs assigned by the
+city-map integrator alongside the streetscape library. Each8×8 graphic selects one
+16-entry4bpp palette. Keep index0 transparent where applicable. Reuse the immutable
+General primary tiles/palettes for the ground behind transparent building pixels.
+Do not replace global General or Pewter palettes simply to accommodate this asset.
+
+Suggested production RGB values are quantized multiples of8, not measurements
+sampled from the photograph:
+
+- Brick: dark(160,72,56), mid(200,112,88), light(224,152,112).
+- Stone: warm(240,216,168), highlight(248,240,208).
+- Slate: dark(48,56,64), mid(72,88,104), light(112,128,136).
+- Glass: dark(32,48,64), mid(88,128,144).
+- Canopy: dark olive(120,128,88), light(160,160,112).
+- Tower accent: dark green(40,64,56), muted green(168,184,160).
+
+## Study generation and acceptance
+
+The exact built-in `image_gen` prompt is in `generation-prompt.txt`. Use the official
+frontal image as architecture input and native screenshot as rendering input.
+Request true transparency and a1536×1024 canvas representing the192×128 logical
+image at8× enlargement. This is a study request; exact output dimensions, uniform
+pixel grid, color count and deduplicated tile counts must be measured afterward.
+
+Accept the design for native conversion only after checking:
+
+1. Clock, roof, brick/stone, arched center and low-wing silhouette match the references.
+2. Entire building fits the proposed envelope; entrance and clear approaches agree.
+3. Pixel clusters remain legible at192×128; no photo-like blur, labels or scene backdrop.
+4. Alpha, palette banks and per-tile16-color limits are valid; no unwanted color spill.
+5. Deduplicated unique graphics and metatiles fit the agreed budgets alongside the kit.
+6. Closed/open door visuals, collisions and returned player position are tested in ROM.
+
+An attractive generated image alone does not satisfy items4–6. Keep the study's
+native-ready status false until indexed conversion, registration and playtesting
+have actually succeeded.
+
+## First study result
+
+The built-in image generation call produced `old-station-study-v1.png` under
+`artifacts/worktrees/c291d4842985/landmark-art/`. It follows the photographed clock
+tower, slate roofs, red/cream facade, arched center and low canopy, and is a useful
+architectural direction study. No creative raster edits or native registrations
+were performed afterward. The exact request remains in `generation-prompt.txt`;
+the measured output and review are recorded in `generation.json`.
+
+The output is1536×1024 RGBA as requested, with761,031 fully transparent pixels.
+It also has255 alpha levels, no fully opaque pixels,105,423 distinct visible RGBA
+values and a soft halo. None of its13,383 aligned8×8 blocks containing visible
+pixels is a uniform logical pixel. Therefore it does not yet satisfy the requested
+192×128 indexed grid, binary alpha, palette or tile-packing requirements. The
+existing game still uses the original placeholder. This image must be described
+as a study, not as an in-game screenshot or accepted native sprite.
