+# City save and Station checkpoint
+
+Save version **2** uses reserved variable `0x40F7`. Existing allocations remain
+`40F8` wild preference, `40F9` trainer-sight preference, `40FA` ten-gym mask,
+`40FB` language, `40FC` chosen starter species and `40FD` tea quest. The upgrade
+does not reselect a team or change the player's Pokémon, bag, language,
+exploration preferences, common-level state, stamps, or other saved variables.
+
+New games use version 2 and the outdoor Station checkpoint `(30,66)`. The native
+whiteout routine retains its normal money loss and party healing. A city
+checkpoint then returns through the normal field fade, without running a
+Pokémon Center nurse script against an outdoor NPC.
+
+## Version 1 to 2: Station art and cached map view
+
+Native Save stores a viewport in `SaveBlock2.mapView`. Continue overlays those
+cached cells on the authored layout. A version-1 save outside the Station can
+therefore overwrite the new facade and collision with its old placeholder.
+Merely zeroing that cache is insufficient: the non-UBFIX native emptiness test
+reads beyond the cache array and can still decide to overlay its zero words.
+
+The bounded upgrade uses the engine's existing full Continue-warp path. In Old
+City it requests the **same actual saved position** from `SaveBlock1.pos`, with
+warp ID -1. It does not use `location.x/y`, which describe the last entrance and
+can be stale. Continue may initially read its old viewport, but the pending
+warp then reloads the complete authored map before exposing the field. No
+fieldmap/cache-engine change is required.
+
+Only six formerly passable cells became solid with this Station art: `(31,57)`,
+`(32,57)`, and `(26,61)` through `(26,64)`. A player saved on one of these cells
+uses the clear Station plaza `(30,66)` instead. Other valid Old City positions,
+including the canonical `(30,66)` save and the garden, are retained.
+
+A pre-existing native Continue warp already causes a full map reload and is
+preserved. An explicit Old City coordinate target on one of those six newly
+blocked cells is repaired to the safe plaza. Version-1 saves in other maps are
+not relocated; their native checkpoint and pending return remain intact. Only
+the version marker is updated there. Current version-2 and future-version saves
+are left untouched. The upgrade is persisted on the next native Save.
+
+## Earlier unversioned prototypes
+
+Unversioned Taichung saves with a party and a recognized four-starter marker
+still upgrade once. The earliest fixed-Bulbasaur prototype is recognized by its
+nonzero tea marker. Saves in the thirteen original city maps retain their
+position; Old City also takes the viewport-refresh path above. Older prototype
+areas use the existing Continue warp to arrive at the Station. An unset legacy
+language becomes English; Chinese remains Chinese. An untouched vanilla
+FireRed save has neither prototype marker and is not migrated. Empty-party
+saves are not migrated. A new game retains its mandatory language/team flow.
+
+ROM-specific browser snapshots deliberately use different namespaces. To move
+progress between ROM revisions, export/import the native `.sav`, then choose
+native Continue.
+
+## Validation
+
+`bash tools/taichung_gameplay/test-save.sh` compiles the actual migration module
+with native-save host stubs. Regression cases cover canonical Station `(30,66)`,
+all six newly blocked cells, seven safe positions (with stale entrance/warp
+coordinates), non-Station city/welcome/legacy maps, pre-existing native return
+warps, all four earlier starter paths and fixed Bulbasaur, one-time behavior,
+current/future versions, empty parties, and untouched vanilla saves. Protected
+variables and opaque team/bag bytes are compared against their original values.
+The tests assert a native full-reload request rather than a cache-zeroing
+substitute. Actual old canonical SRAM → native Continue rendering and collision
+acceptance is performed by the integrator after the ROM build.
