+# Native Team selection — first slice
+
+The normal-field Start menu's existing Pokémon row becomes **TEAM / 隊伍**.
+This keeps the nine-row menu within the GBA screen. Link/Union/Safari menus
+retain their original Pokémon action. No save variables, script menu IDs,
+language bridge fields, map geometry or browser source are allocated/changed.
+
+In Team, Up/Down chooses an occupied slot or the first empty slot. A browses
+National Dex 001–150 (Mew excluded); evolved forms are available directly.
+Up/Down changes species, Left/Right skips eight, and L/R skips forty. The
+preview shows level 50 and the species preset. A opens confirmation; a second
+A commits the choice. B at confirmation returns to browsing without writing;
+B at browsing returns to slots. B/Start at slots returns to the field menu.
+SELECT at slots opens the existing native party interface, including Summary,
+Switch and held-item controls; exiting it returns to Team.
+
+`TaichungTeamSetSlot` is the sole new creation operation. It rejects battle
+context, unsupported species, slot seven and party gaps. It constructs a
+player-owned level-50 Pokémon using native `CreateMon`, installs the curated
+preset, preserves an existing held item/mail binding on replacement, then
+copies into the selected native slot. New additions append; replacement does
+not move a displaced Pokémon to the PC. Confirmation is therefore required.
+The newly created partner has full HP/PP and native calculated stats.
+The operation does not write the saved starter marker, language, exploration
+preferences or ten-bit completion field. Saves use the existing native party.
+
+Preset source/validation and honest short sets are documented separately in
+`taichung-team-presets.md`. Pokémon and move names retain native English in
+both locales, matching the current localization scope. Team labels and
+instructions use the existing English/Traditional Chinese preference.
+
+## Shared glyph integration
+
+The exact additional glyph request is `伍使全力加快或更置隊頁`. Isolated
+generation uses the existing parent helper and the full current translation
+corpus, including the city additions. The generated charmap and glyph table
+travel together. Main/localization must regenerate the union if merging with
+another text change; neither generated file should be cherry-picked alone.
+No renderer implementation changes are needed.
+
+## Slice boundary
+
+This first commit provides free party creation/replacement and preset moves.
+It deliberately preserves the current starter-opening level and gym balance
+until the immediately following common-level/preparation change. It does not
+claim all ten leader battles, badge artwork, balance approval, or publication.
+
+Runtime checks and the exact feature-ROM hashes are recorded in the focused
+QA handoff. Feature artifacts stay under the parent ignored directory
+`artifacts/worktrees/3c6cc7b4e276/`; canonical release outputs are untouched.
