+# Native Station loss and checkpoint verification
+
+The controlled loss test passed against the unchanged combined release:
+
+- Source: `a1ff057980cf3480b5552ffbbc6ea4a3beaac9c6`
+- ROM SHA-1: `ae0ada352b1cd0b0d281c09fdde42a95446c9b4f`
+- ROM SHA-256: `629bcd40965e7e5af51c3e1ffbb6fa436f76fe454fbb9f21aa7015e3dd6a2185`
+
+## Controlled fixture
+
+The input was the real pre-gym native save with Pikachu's current HP changed from 19 to 1 and its sector checksum corrected. Comparing the two 131,088-byte files found exactly two changed bytes: HP at `0x308E` and checksum at `0x3FF6`. This is a deliberate HP1 QA fixture, not organic player progress. No other save state or ROM data was edited for the test.
+
+Fixture SHA-256: `a3b3ed2b108646dea8e7c9d7daafb59d6abfeccf05721abd009413c7b7a9d141`.
+
+The read-only save inspector validated matching checksum-correct SaveBlock1 sectors 1 and 2. The game then loaded the file through its actual cartridge Continue menu in a fresh isolated runtime with snapshot restoration disabled. Its initial state was map group 43/map 0, position `(30, 66)`, one level-five Pikachu at 1/19 HP, zero gym stamps, save version 1 and English. Both unset exploration preferences retained their Normal defaults.
+
+## Runtime sequence and result
+
+1. Walked through the Station door, approached JUN and accepted the native Yes/No challenge.
+2. Selected only Growl. On the second turn, the real opposing level-five Rattata used Tackle and reduced Pikachu to 0/19 HP. The game displayed fainting, defeat, its normal money-loss messages and whiteout.
+3. The native whiteout path returned the player to the outdoor Station checkpoint, without a nurse/counter scene. Start and Save controls worked immediately.
+4. Used the actual native Save action before moving. Its summary displayed `GYMS 0/10`. Exported the native SRAM file and inspected it independently.
+5. Walked right and left, re-entered the Station through the real door and approached JUN again. The normal challenge offer and Yes/No menu appeared again; declined it normally. This checks the retry offer without running a second battle.
+
+The post-loss save confirms:
+
+| Value | Before | After native loss/save |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| Save counter | 2 | 3 |
+| Map group / number | 43 / 0 | 43 / 0 |
+| Position | `(30, 66)` | `(30, 66)` |
+| Party | One Pikachu, level 5 | One Pikachu, level 5 |
+| Current / maximum HP | 1 / 19 | 19 / 19 |
+| Status | 0 | 0 |
+| Raw gym-completion mask | 0 | 0 |
+| Save version / language / starter | 1 / 1 / 25 | 1 / 1 / 25 |
+| Wild / trainer-sight raw preferences | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 |
+| Last-heal warp | `(43, 0, -1, 30, 66)` | `(43, 0, -1, 30, 66)` |
+
+The exported save includes the runtime's 16-byte RTC trailer and has SHA-256 `2a4e95ce2fa761b2ea1dddfc32b51a9fac2a486bbfb5008667061154848b64b4`. The advanced save counter distinguishes this native save from the initial fixture. No stamp was awarded for defeat, the party healed, and field/menu/door controls recovered. No engine correction was required.
+
